{
  "_comment": "Breeze TTS 2 vocal-event vocabulary — the single source for the client (tags.py), the server overlay (/v1/capabilities, deployed next to it) and TAGS.md (tests/test_tags.py checks the doc lists every entry). The model has no closed tag list and no tag tokens: tags are plain text it learned in training, so this records what is documented and what was measured, not what is allowed. Status (measured on goldielocks, 2026-10-07, 107 cases, ASR-scored): verified = performed and audible (ASR or ear); accepted = never read aloud, effect plausible but unverified by ear; harmful = derails generation, don't use; pending = not measured.",
  "control_token_pattern": "<\\|AUDIO\\|>|<\\|audio_eos\\|>",
  "inline_token_pattern": "\\[S\\d\\]|<ins_(?:bos|eos)>",
  "english_bracket_event_pattern": "\\[([A-Za-z][A-Za-z '\\-]*)\\]",
  "tiers": {
    "documented": "Named in the open-weights model card and upstream README (the open-weights model's own examples).",
    "hosted": "BreezeBlue's 34-event list for its hosted model (docs.breezeblue.ai/guides/audio-tags); status on the open weights is per local validation.",
    "experimental": "Other spellings people reach for; free-form text the model may or may not perform."
  },
